### Cost Efficiency Analysis
**Source:** Multiple sources
**Snapshot:** 2026

DeepSeek V4.1 Flash's real cost efficiency depends on:
- Prompt caching usage (98% cost reduction on input tokens)
- Off-peak vs peak hours usage
- Batch API usage (not specified)
- Effort level selection (higher effort = more thinking tokens = higher cost)
- Task complexity and length
- Context length (1M tokens)
- Task type (agentic workloads benefit from memory features)

The model is positioned as DeepSeek's flagship general-purpose model for agentic coding, vision, and high-throughput applications. The cache-read pricing is 98% cheaper than standard input pricing ($0.006 vs $0.30 per 1M tokens), cutting typical workload costs by approximately 98% and highly agentic workloads by up to 99%.

